dirname - extract the directory part of a pathname

SYNOPSIS
    dirname path

DESCRIPTION
    Strip trailing slashes and the last pathname component. A relative path
    with no directory component gives a dot. The root directory is
    represented by a single slash. The operation works on the spelling of
    the pathname.

SEE ALSO
    basename(1), pwd(1)
